# An argument too many is a mistake as well: a subcommand that takes none
# quietly ignoring one would hide a caller that thinks it is asking for
# something.
run available now
exit 2
file tasks/M1-01.md
	---
	id: M1-01
	depends_on: []
	exclusive: no
	---
stderr
	usage: tasks.sh available
	       tasks.sh claim <task-id>
	       tasks.sh sweep
	       tasks.sh release <task-id> <commit> <last-seen>
	       tasks.sh check
